      "content": "I am currently refining the advanced aerodynamics module for our flight instructor training program. I need to ensure we have a technically rigorous explanation of how the Kutta condition facilitates the development of circulation around an airfoil, and how this circulation is fundamentally responsible for the pressure differential described by Bernoulli's principle. \n\nCould you provide a professional, detailed breakdown of this process, specifically focusing on how the stagnation point at the trailing edge ensures a smooth flow and the subsequent establishment of circulatory flow? Please keep the explanation suitable for a professional curriculum.",
